  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/elekto-com-br/cnpj-cpf",
  "published": "2026-11-12T00:46:05.337Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v1.4.2: Cnpj.IsValid and Cnpj.TryParse now trim the whitespace around a CNPJ, as the constructor already did, so that a CNPJ padded past 18 characters, as in a fixed-width field, is valid through all three. Cpf now trims whitespace and NUL around a CPF in any format, and through a span as well, where it used to accept surrounding spaces only on an unformatted string of up to 14 characters, and takes a plus sign anywhere as punctuation, as it did the minus. Cpf no longer depends on the current culture: 1.4.1 also took a sign in the culture's own form, such as the U+2212 minus of Swedish, and now only + and - count; apart from that, no input that 1.4.1 accepted is rejected. Trimming allocates nothing, and validating an unformatted CPF takes about a third less time.",
